{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":72307,"duration_api_ms":109845,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"62876a94-cc83-412e-a48f-1f2ffee5e723","total_cost_usd":0.36558640000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":385,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24563,"cache_read_input_tokens":77261,"output_tokens":2347,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24563,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":105,"outputTokens":5024,"cacheReadInputTokens":385884,"cacheCreationInputTokens":39219,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11283715000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":385,"outputTokens":2347,"cacheReadInputTokens":77261,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24563,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.25274925,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accepted one maintainability amendment (misleading template name). Rejected four: one proposes weakening a clear behavioral assertion with speculative tolerance; three have factually incorrect premises — the file is already tracked, the constant is already unified with a regression test, and the Element::Alkalinity branch does not exist.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-5a2e1e96","decision":"reject","rationale":"The assertion `<= initial_total` is a clear behavioral invariant: a neglected tank should not end with more shrimp than it started with. The flakiness concern is speculative and depends on hypothetical model retuning. Adding a +2 tolerance weakens the regression's ability to catch real growth bugs in the neglected path. If peak tracking proves insufficient under future model changes, the fix should be better sampling, not a looser bound."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-87d566aa","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the VS-07 bare-bottom arm at line 1034 passes \"medium_planted\" as the scenario template despite overriding plant_selection to None. This is functionally correct but misleading to anyone reading the test without tracing through the override chain. A brief comment explaining the intentional reuse of the planted template as a controlled baseline would cost nothing and prevent future confusion."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-beaf754d","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's premise is factually wrong. `git ls-files crates/tank_core/tests/nitrification_alkalinity.rs` confirms the file is already tracked in version control. The tests will run in CI as expected."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-c6a42041","decision":"reject","rationale":"The inconsistency described no longer exists. The preset path uses `default_alk_per_mg_n()` which returns `NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N` — the same constant used in `ProcessParams::default()`. Furthermore, a dedicated regression test at presets.rs:3322-3329 asserts they match within 1e-12 tolerance. Both the fix and the guard are already in place."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-4fc13edd","decision":"reject","rationale":"The `Element` enum in budget_helpers.rs contains only Nitrogen, Carbon, and Oxygen — there is no Alkalinity variant. A comment at lines 66-68 explicitly states that alkalinity (meq-based) is intentionally excluded from this mg-based N/C/O ledger. The amendment is fixing a code path that does not exist."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"597ddab8-b784-4c58-ab2f-5aaee234cdbd"}
